{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>For with joy you shall go out.</b> From the exile." "<b>You shall be carried.</b> To your land on horses and mules, [if] regarding the exile of Babylon, so it was; and if for the future, it is explicit at the end of the book (Isaiah 66:20). Some say he spoke of two exiles." "<b>They shall clap.</b> Like the meaning of יכו (they shall strike), and this expression is known in Aramaic, and from the root of ומחה אל כתף ים כנרת (Numbers 34:11)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {1 "The bracketed [אם] appears in the Hebrew source; rendered as conditional 'if.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:48.849917723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}